      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T08:15:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003d ?\n\nPreviously, \u003e is used because if the condition is not true, the logic won\u0027t be triggered, and `avrcp_version` variable will be left alone, \n\nAfter your change, if this condition is false, the code can fallback to the else if condition, which changes the logic of dealing with devices that makes interop_match_addr() returns true. \n\nPlease leave a comment about this, too\n\nHowever, if it is your intended behavior, it is fine. In that case, please comment about your design by adding it to the LOG message.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1249,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1249,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "72b1174a4f314f73f2c9c0efee2434fb8ebeba0d",
